eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\n- From the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -(-2) & 5\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=5$ and $\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=-2.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda =5+(-2)\\text{i}=5-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix $P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3+0\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda ,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n$$\n\\lambda =5∓2\\text{i},\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39130/selection/ma-v1/8fb47d7893336ae8c925a2aa8be3f7bc4484fd7d54fe3a083b4e595844430ca7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-99329/selection/9011d0ebfaf697415bcd3b94ba7f631e89e3b82665746bf727eeb3b2089f4ed9" :answer/id #uuid "a684839d-472a-576e-9042-3d04f501c9d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =4∓\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ -3∓\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99329/selection/09d79eab12f5dcc90ac905b863ee208b4b034a78192209f90b1a0312c8e477a0" :answer/id #uuid "2bedcedd-1148-504a-a326-d1556153fc35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =2∓\\text{i}$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}4\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ ∓2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db