e904fdcaa7a58317d9d0ba1a6a7d4605cd035f" "q-39132/selection/87ddccc7dadfc54b694ca564186eb1618389cb642a1f028f943e2282d878c1ec" "q-39132/selection/c47cabac0c62229f8d4991ee59467bb1b29456cc77eab570d3e8ce63b7ae4c33" "q-39132/selection/5a5bc55d5583dfed2a155ad562472be29e74caeb1bd3b19a335b147ddd6fdf32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39132" :question/id #uuid "7f3fa040-fe21-5249-b083-19346af531bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-39132" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ what are the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors of $A?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\n- From the matrix $C=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ -(-2) & -7\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=-7$ and $\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=-2.$ So, our eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-7+(-2)\\text{i}=-7-2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n- From the matrix $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ we deduce that our corresponding eigenvector is\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1+(-2)\\text{i} \\\\ -3+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-2\\text{i} \\\\ -3+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda ,$ and the second eigenvector must be the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nTherefore, our eigenvalues and eigenvectors are \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-7∓2\\text{i},\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1∓2\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1dcdd3f4-c03e-5887-a493-05598dbe4fc3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494/selection/c5d66d552f0f14593afc4532759e003d67d9c37574e4cbdbe430cf29e5c7d106" :answer/id #uuid "3f065a62-494d-5897-98c5-77f62246f7bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494/selection/909e9c38b1d7d56f006a274e53829b998a0f5185911029523d7af6256df0db3d" :answer/id #uuid "dc53647b-1875-5d3f-b511-5ed29dd653e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494/selection/33ec7f97dc47d8a6c3e0932fa183884046306b4a09941e28698f56850fd18c27" :answer/id #uuid "1e905837-05cd-5930-b5d5-a8736fcd68df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494/selection/47e7e3556c49b4f23699967206817faabc443061a9763ee44ce66f4545196a2a" :answer/id #uuid "cd1439c8-fdc4-5236-bf01-4122ff8ff749" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494/selection/b61e411d4469bbbd46be3a31272fe81f07c73140b47885907ec58fdf761a1ef1" :answer/id #uuid "8bc7a5ce-153b-5ee3-bff6-e9f8a921feec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "df0b3567-f146-5ada-98da-b9bb5e66153f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140494/selection/33ec7f97dc47d8a6c3e0932fa183884046306b4a09941e28698f56850fd18c27" :answer-field/choices ["q-140494/selection/c5d66d552f0f14593afc4532759e003d67d9c37574e4cbdbe430cf29e5c7d106" "q-140494/selection/909e9c38b1d7d56f006a274e53829b998a0f5185911029523d7af6256df0db3d" "q-140494/selection/33ec7f97dc47d8a6c3e0932fa183884046306b4a09941e28698f56850fd18c27" "q-140494/selection/47e7e3556c49b4f23699967206817faabc443061a9763ee44ce66f4545196a2a" "q-140494/selection/b61e411d4469bbbd46be3a31272fe81f07c73140b47885907ec58fdf761a1ef1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140494" :question/id #uuid "4820017f-1059-531a-a643-9f08294cdd17" :question/math-academy-id "q-140494" :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2-3\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140494/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b049dea4-5045-57ec-ad6a-c49f30e5da1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140494"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496/selection/9b487356aae5d293839ac109a094edb1613231c129dc80b8da0173fd548c0d2c" :answer/id #uuid "866dcc81-ff13-5365-ae25-d0cda937abd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496/selection/c06f16af590f90c028f79c06437310dde562307245e0e461a9471d0aa580792a" :answer/id #uuid "6c9da745-f68b-5ddc-8540-28551e3018d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496/selection/720ef992145f63cfd47df21442b6e956af633fb0cf7b7cb82e6b5140b6028989" :answer/id #uuid "5764f478-5291-567a-85bd-08c0b7fbc141" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496/selection/1f8791c7b7cbd76846b7bac3ba5fc7cd1c625c967a4f3e11a8bd77a44bad2be2" :answer/id #uuid "ed39a372-881a-5887-b603-d88e943dae07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496/selection/6538ad93d73b5a52595d7adc547db822452d363237e1eafb7ce8928a4bfe7bb6" :answer/id #uuid "b608f9a8-f0d6-5353-b03b-37080949693c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a00122d-5c88-5cb5-b76e-9fceadb27bdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140496/selection/9b487356aae5d293839ac109a094edb1613231c129dc80b8da0173fd548c0d2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-140496/selection/9b487356aae5d293839ac109a094edb1613231c129dc80b8da0173fd548c0d2c" "q-140496/selection/c06f16af590f90c028f79c06437310dde562307245e0e461a9471d0aa580792a" "q-140496/selection/720ef992145f63cfd47df21442b6e956af633fb0cf7b7cb82e6b5140b6028989" "q-140496/selection/1f8791c7b7cbd76846b7bac3ba5fc7cd1c625c967a4f3e11a8bd77a44bad2be2" "q-140496/selection/6538ad93d73b5a52595d7adc547db822452d363237e1eafb7ce8928a4bfe7bb6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140496" :question/id #uuid "5605d4ea-f418-59f0-ade2-398cf6d0d3af" :question/math-academy-id "q-140496" :question/problem "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-7 \\\\ 4\\text{i}+3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =7+4\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nNext, we can find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-7 \\\\ 4\\text{i}+3\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140496/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b049dea4-5045-57ec-ad6a-c49f30e5da1f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39127/selection/f4c7782d59b87a4cd5a178259629ad923b8940bf61c364a9838e7b6bc1e029ce" :answer/id #uuid "15eaa558-b6a6-5f09-aa8a-5bdceeb778c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39127/selection/c9199ab2ff7e106a7516a90c3267a32dcf0a7a40cdab221a963d952cf8f82266" :answer/id #uuid "60514111-792d-5512-80b9-63bd27c452e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39127/selection/37d276adf1651f780b00172aaca4557c581aa63dfc342e7f8e62793c2c96d51a" :answer/id #uuid "8034835a-2b0f-55d7-9ec4-415aaf887139" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39127/selection/c105f69ec04a19f822947b1c41439bed48fde8146d78aadcdb2c261dc01823b8" :answer/id #uuid "4cc7fb6a-2718-5fa2-a920-7fd77434323f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39127/selection/abfc562aa415a5291adfcaf808455ef0a2f855524330aab37c6a9e6e611be6d5" :answer/id #uuid "d801348a-ea00-5ee8-af5e-3f73c251bc9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39127/selection" :ans