& \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=3+2\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-99412/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88f3ba21-6407-503e-aec0-fa4462a69e73"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-99428/selection/494c1e7a570120885866051ae0977cf50fd39ccac2fb1458f934cc7dccfee0a3" :answer/id #uuid "43aa2b39-220a-5429-892d-4e5b03fe4c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -6 \\\\ 8 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99428/selection/e7a52a666c5199e9ac020f0633db68023ad816ce451037bc26d63136baa34214" :answer/id #uuid "8b2170d7-e6aa-513f-a145-cfb5fe29722e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99428/selection/b73a12331c73682b2c1447f107c62dfa99e6a58f1564c370c123aa099e599c65" :answer/id #uuid "7d66e372-1f5a-5515-ac9e-ccb417d75a8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/v